│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a cost-aware multicast-tree       │
│                          │ heuristic. The new search builds candidate shared delivery trees: the union of            │
│                          │ independent shortest paths and several greedy directed Steiner-style trees seeded by each │
│                          │ destination. It selects the tree with the lowest unique edge cost, then derives           │
│                          │ source-to-destination paths from that shared tree for every partition. This preserves     │
│                          │ parallel partition delivery while allowing common trunk links to be transferred once and  │
│                          │ forwarded to multiple destinations, substantially reducing redundant inter-cloud transfer │
│                          │ charges.                                                                                  │
