│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces independent per-destination shortest paths with a cost-aware │
│                          │ multicast growth tree. It is inspired by shortest-path routing from the original program, │
│                          │ but uses a fundamentally different incremental Steiner-style broadcast strategy.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm grows a shared directed delivery backbone from the source. At each step it  │
│                          │ evaluates all unreached destinations using a multi-source shortest-path search rooted at  │
│                          │ already-reached tree nodes. Existing tree edges have zero incremental cost, which         │
│                          │ strongly favors routes that reuse previously installed transfer links. A bounded-detour   │
│                          │ rule ensures that sharing does not produce excessively expensive routes compared with the │
│                          │ destination's direct shortest path.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Once the shared tree is built, every destination receives its source-to-destination route │
│                          │ through that tree for every partition. This minimizes redundant edge installation while   │
│                          │ preserving the original `BroadCastTopology` output format.                                │
