│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_multicast_tree                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with a greedy shared multicast-tree    │
│                          │ construction. The previous implementation finds a complete source-to-destination route    │
│                          │ separately for every destination, which can repeatedly pay for the same expensive         │
│                          │ inter-cloud links.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new search grows a directed broadcast tree from the source. At each step it chooses   │
│                          │ the unserved destination whose route has the smallest incremental cost when               │
│                          │ already-selected tree edges are treated as free. This preserves previously transferred    │
│                          │ data on shared links, naturally favors overlapping routes, and only adds new network      │
│                          │ segments when necessary. Each destination still receives a complete source-to-destination │
│                          │ path for every partition, so the existing BroadCastTopology interface remains unchanged.  │
│                          │ Edges without a valid numeric cost are excluded rather than causing Dijkstra failures.    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0225                                                                                   │
