│ patch_name               │ unrestricted_shared_tree_growth                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Remove the per-destination detour guard when growing the broadcast tree. The optimization │
│                          │ target is the total cost of unique network edges used to distribute the input, not the    │
│                          │ individual unicast path length to each destination. Once a transfer reaches any tree      │
│                          │ node, extending from that node only incurs the cost of newly installed edges; rejecting a │
│                          │ low incremental-cost branch because its end-to-end route is longer can discard the most   │
│                          │ economical multicast plan.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The source shortest path remains implicitly available as a candidate at every iteration,  │
│                          │ so all reachable destinations can still be attached. Selecting by incremental edge cost   │
│                          │ directly aligns the greedy expansion with minimizing redundant cross-cloud transfers.     │
