│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_broadcast_tree                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single locally-greedy broadcast-tree construction with a multi-start          │
│                          │ directed-Steiner heuristic. The current greedy expansion always commits to the cheapest   │
│                          │ first destination extension, which can prevent selection of a slightly more expensive     │
│                          │ initial trunk that later serves many clouds at low incremental cost.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The revised logic evaluates the existing greedy solution plus one seeded solution for     │
│                          │ every reachable destination. Each seeded solution installs that destination’s least-cost  │
│                          │ source path first, then continues using zero-cost reuse of installed broadcast edges. The │
│                          │ lowest total unique-edge-cost tree is selected. This retains valid source-rooted paths    │
│                          │ and shared-edge semantics while reducing sensitivity to destination ordering and          │
│                          │ improving opportunities for overlapping inter-cloud transfers.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
