│ patch_name               │ multistart_broadcast_tree                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the order-sensitive single greedy expansion with a deterministic multi-start      │
│                          │ shared-tree search. The current algorithm always attaches the destination with the        │
│                          │ cheapest immediate extension first; that can consume a cheap branch point and prevent a   │
│                          │ slightly more expensive initial trunk from unlocking substantially lower-cost fan-out to  │
│                          │ the remaining clouds.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement evaluates the normal greedy construction plus one construction seeded by  │
│                          │ each reachable destination. Each construction still charges an edge only once, so it      │
│                          │ preserves broadcast sharing and overlapping transfer opportunities. Selecting the         │
│                          │ least-cost installed-edge set reduces redundant inter-cloud transfers while retaining a   │
│                          │ source-rooted directed topology that can be materialized for every partition.             │
