│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses a greedy multicast-tree expansion, varying only the first       │
│                          │ destination seed. Its key configuration is an implicit single-pass greedy selection that  │
│                          │ can miss a globally cheaper shared relay/trunk.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version uses an exact directed-Steiner dynamic program for up to 11 unique reachable │
│                          │ destinations (`EXACT_TERMINAL_LIMIT = 11`). The DP evaluates all destination subsets and  │
│                          │ all possible relay nodes, allowing multiple destination branches to merge at low-cost     │
│                          │ intermediate clouds before being connected to the source. This reduces redundant          │
│                          │ source-side transfers and finds globally optimal shared broadcast trees on typical        │
│                          │ multi-cloud destination sets.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For larger sets, it falls back to a deterministic shared-aware greedy attachment strategy │
│                          │ with zero marginal cost for already-installed broadcast edges. Invalid, missing,          │
│                          │ negative, and non-finite costs are excluded safely. All partitions retain the same        │
│                          │ selected shared tree paths, allowing parallel partition transfer over the chosen          │
│                          │ multi-network topology.                                                                   │
