│ patch_name               │ directed_steiner_broadcast                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace independent per-destination shortest paths with an exact directed-Steiner         │
│                          │ broadcast tree solver for typical broadcast sizes. The dynamic program jointly selects    │
│                          │ relay nodes and shared prefix links, so a transfer sent once from the source can fan out  │
│                          │ at low-cost intermediate clouds instead of paying for redundant source-to-destination     │
│                          │ routes. It uses reverse multi-source Dijkstra relaxation to account for the cheapest      │
│                          │ route from every possible relay to each terminal subset, reconstructs the selected shared │
│                          │ arborescence, and writes each destination’s path through that common topology. For        │
│                          │ unusually large destination sets, it falls back to a multi-source greedy attachment       │
│                          │ strategy that still reuses already-reached nodes and links.                               │
