│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces independent shortest paths with a directed Steiner-tree      │
│                          │ approach. For small destination sets, it uses an exact subset dynamic program that finds  │
│                          │ a minimum-cost shared broadcast arborescence rooted at the source. Shared relay links are │
│                          │ paid for once and reused by every destination, substantially reducing redundant           │
│                          │ inter-cloud transfers.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For larger destination sets, it falls back to a marginal-cost multicast heuristic that    │
│                          │ repeatedly attaches the destination requiring the least additional network cost to the    │
│                          │ existing broadcast tree. All resulting shared tree paths are expanded into the existing   │
│                          │ `BroadCastTopology` interface for every partition.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
