│                          │ edges that are no longer needed after their paths are unioned. Removing expensive edges   │
│                          │ whenever every reachable destination remains source-reachable reduces the evaluator’s     │
│                          │ shared physical-link cost without changing delivery coverage, partition paths, or         │
│                          │ source-rooted topology semantics. Processing edges from highest to lowest cost maximizes  │
│                          │ savings first while retaining a valid broadcast route to every terminal.                  │
